    isbefore: []  # 9dc3
    duplicate_of: []  # 9dc3
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9dc3
    pr_ref:  # 9dc3
    description: "pony: behaviours (`be`) are not extracted, so an actor's message handlers are not symbols and calls inside them are credited to the actor.\n\nFOUND 2026-09-25 by the docstring-staleness audit (reviewer aside), REPRODUCED on the production path (`analyze_pony`):\n\n    actor Main\n      new create(env: Env) => None\n      be ping() => helper()\n      fun helper() => None\n\n    symbols: Main (actor), Main.create (constructor), Main.helper (method) -- no Main.ping\n    calls Main(actor, 1-9) -> Main.helper      <- should be Main.ping -> Main.helper\n\nMECHANISM: the member walk handles only (\"constructor\", \"method\") node types; the grammar parses `be` as a `behavior` node, which is skipped. Behaviours are the actor model's entry points (asynchronous message handlers), so this hides every actor's receive surface, and the module docstring claims message passing is understood.\n\nFix direction: extract `behavior` nodes as symbols (kind to be decided against the registry: method, with a meta flag, is the likely fit) and credit their calls to them."  # 9dc3
    fields: {}  # 9dc3
- op: discuss  # b009
  at: '2026-10-04T10:36:27Z'  # b009
  by: agent  # b009
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b009
  clock: 2  # b009
  nonce: b009  # b009
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-04 (stage 8b agent). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/binap (worktree ~/hg_wt/binap, based on stage-8 integration 2a98abb55d, NOT pushed), commit 829ef03b24. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/binap.md.\n\nPremise re-verified at 2a98abb55d (live repro, analyze_pony): no symbol for be; Main(actor) -> Main.helper for a call in be ping. ALSO FOUND: the enclosing callable was looked up by NAME in the repository-wide registry, so with two files declaring actor Main / new create, one file's calls were credited to the other file's Main.create (INV-midag); and callee resolution preferred whichever file the registry kept.\n\nFix: behaviour = kind=method + meta.is_behaviour=True (registered on symbol_meta; schema.json regenerated; spec symbol_meta count 54 -> 55) + signature \"be name(params)\"; type meta gains behaviour_count. Enclosing callable / type by POSITION via core enclosing_declared_symbol over the file's declarations; a callee resolves to this file's declaration first; the bare-call own-type fallback (helper() -> Main.helper) is file-local. pony moves to VERIFIED in the extended1 call-anchor gate.\n\nTests: red then green (see binap.md); final targeted run 333 passed; scoped coverage 100%.\n\nA/B on ponyc (no Pony repo exists in ~/whole_bunch_of_repos; shallow clone 44f94baea5, 1,388 files): 687 behaviour symbols; containment violations 4,420 -> 0; on single-call lines 1,422 calls moved onto a behaviour, 3,325 from another file's same-named callable to this file's, 406 from the type / a wrong same-named method to the containing callable; callees: 1,851 sites that bound into another file's same-named type now unresolved, 254 rebound to this file, 220 now resolve to a behaviour. Edge count unchanged.\n\nResidual filed: WI-bifat (a call on a call result loses its receiver; surfaced a false self-binding once behaviours became symbols)."  # b009
